    "statementMarkdown": "Let $A B C$ be a triangle with $A B>A C$. The internal angle bisector of $\\angle B A C$ intersects the side $B C$ at $D$. The circles with diameters $B D$ and $C D$ intersect the circumcircle of $\\triangle A B C$ a second time at $P \\neq B$ and $Q \\neq C$, respectively. The lines $P Q$ and $B C$ intersect at $X$. Prove that $A X$ is tangent to the circumcircle of $\\triangle A B C$.\n",
